Enable Banking is not configured for this deployment.

This file is committed to git and contains no key material -- it exists
only so compose.yaml's read-only bind mount always has a valid host-side
source, which lets `docker compose up` succeed for deployments that
intentionally leave Enable Banking unconfigured (its RSA private key
resolver already fails closed on anything that doesn't parse as a real
PEM, so this placeholder can never be mistaken for a working key even if
somehow read).

To enable Enable Banking, set both of the following in your .env (never in
this file, never in compose.yaml, never committed to git):

  ENABLE_BANKING_APPLICATION_ID=<your application id>
  ENABLE_BANKING_PRIVATE_KEY_HOST_FILE=/absolute/path/to/your/real-key.pem

See .env.example for the full explanation.
